  "footnote": "Major courses require B- or better and cannot be S/U. Up to two FREN courses taught in English and up to two Cornell courses outside Romance Studies may count if at least 50% of their content deals directly with France or the Francophone world. Up to three non-Cornell courses, including study abroad, may count under the same 50% content rule; instruction in French alone is insufficient. These language, content and origin limits require advisor review; outside-subject and transfer substitutions are not automatically recognized. Study abroad expects FREN 2095 before departure; a 3000-level Romance Studies course is recommended. Optional honors requires a 3.00 overall GPA, 3.5 major GPA, independent research ability, an essay available by April 15 and an oral examination. FREN 4290 and FREN 4300 honors credit is additional to the eight major courses."
